# The two hard dependencies of this mod, named here because the shared table in
# scripts/stage-pickle-wsl.sh does not know their Workshop ids, and a dependency it cannot place
# stops the run before anything is launched ("no Workshop id known for ...").
#
# This is NOT a set of optional mods, and the pass it serves is still the one WITHOUT any: both
# lines below are declared in Mod/About/About.xml under modDependencies and would be staged anyway
# if the script could find them. The file is named wsl-deps.sans-facultatifs.map so that the pass
# engraves its own true name in the report (-pickle-set-name reads it off the file name), and so
# that it has to be picked explicitly: Run-PickleWsl.ps1 passes 'none' when no -DepMap is given.
#
#   -DepMap wsl-deps.sans-facultatifs.map
#
# Staged twice - once as a dependency, once as an overlay entry - which the game tolerates: the
# same arrangement carried AdaptiveStorageNeolithicRenew through three runs on 2026-09-21.
#
# packageId                      workshopId
Mlie.MMDrumcanMOD                3417093756   # the drum bath, and Hed_BathingAtDrumBathPassive
Dubwise.DubsBadHygiene           836308268    # the hygiene need, DubDef.SoakingWet, the bath memories
